{\fldrslt{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ul\cf1 TranQuangKhai}}}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0
\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 /Pxiabay]}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0
\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 When asked by at least three journalists why posts authored by Mikkelson\u8217 s ex-wife now carried his byline, Mikkelson explained that it had been auto-populated during the migration. \u8220 That\u8217 s so typically David,\u8221  LaCapria, now content manager at Snopes, says laughing. \u8220 There\u8217 s this grain of truth, and this whole fluffy lie wrapped around it.\u8221 }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Snopes had staffed up and was doing well, though. It was even regarded as a sleeper media story. \u8220 For at least a year, everything was humming along,\u8221  Binkowski says. \u8220 We were all getting raises. Traffic was great. It was a unicorn place.\u8221 }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 There were death threats \'e0 gogo. Some people were unshakeable in their conviction that Snopes was an agent of the far left. Bankrolled by George Soros, in the tank for Obummer and hiLIARy. But the real threat that emerged, according to Mikkelson and Green, was its partial owners, Richmond and Schoentrup.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 \u8220 Butch Cassidy and the Sundance Kid, that\u8217 s them,\u8221  Mikkelson told me when we spoke all those years back.}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum
\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Proper Media had an oceanview office in San Diego, which local Snopes employees were allowed free use of. That changed at the beginning of 2017, when Richmond and Schoentrup were in Puerto Rico, where they said they were relocating for the tax break, and Mikkelson canceled Proper Media\u8217 s vendor contract. (He said they weren\u8217 t doing their job.) As owners of a chunk of Snopes, Richmond and Schoentrup did not believe he had the right, and, effectively, withheld the site\u8217 s ad revenue, according to Mikkelson and Green, taking its backend \u8220 hostage.\u8221  In turn, they launched a GoFundMe campaign titled \u8220 Save Our Snopes\u8221  (#fightforfacts), the goal mark of which would grow to $2 million. The money was for legal fees, operating expenses, and \u8220 the continuation of our overall mission to fight misinformation.\u8221 }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Richmond and Schoentrup sued in May 2017 over subterfuge and mismanagement, and a protracted legal battle ensued, but neither the court of public opinion nor the press seemed to seriously entertain the possibility that these guys were in the right and the heads of a fact-checking house might not be the good guys after all. \u8220 They\u8217 re winning the narrative,\u8221  said Schoentrup. \u8220 It\u8217 s Snopes. Snopes can tell no lie.\u8221 \~(Snopes gave up its foothold in the San Diego office around the time the suit was filed and became a remote company.)}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Another major moment came months later in 2017, when Mikkelson and Green fired Binkowski, the site\u8217 s managing editor. The discord traces back, at least partly, to a splashy agreement Snopes had made with Facebook one year prior, to help quash misinformation on the social media platform. Binkowski had sensed that the tech giant was pushing false stories and using Snopes\u8217  brand for crisis PR. She fought the partnership: \u8220 We cannot be their bitch. We cannot accurately report on people we\u8217 re taking money from,\u8221  she told me she\u8217 d argued. Mikkelson and Green disagreed, at least at first. Snopes eventually did end the agreement but not until 2019, by which time Binkowski was long gone. \u8220 [Binkowski] worked seven days a week, from like 8 a.m. to 7 p.m.,\u8221  editing up to 15 stories a day, LaCapria recalled with disgust. \u8220 She was underpaid and overworked, and ruthlessly discarded.\u8221 }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Mikkelson and Green were bullying LaCapria too, according to both LaCapria and a recent staffer who spoke on condition of anonymity. In December 2017, LaCapria\u8217 s husband passed away in his sleep while abroad. \u8220 David was initially very nice about it, and he arranged for me to get a standby ticket to go to England,\u8221  for the funeral, she said. But Mikkelson then pressured her to \u8220 come back to work sooner\u8212 which I did on January 22, 2018.\u8221 }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Her relationship with Mikkelson worsened: \u8220 I think he was uncomfortable with my initially hysterical shock and that\u8217 s when he started being acrimonious,\u8221  LaCapria says. Around June 2018, Mikkelson became \u8220 livid for no clear reason,\u8221  she says, relegating her to \u8220 secretarial duties.\u8221  LaCapria soon resigned and, together with Arturo Garcia\u8212 another former Snopes reporter, who has a pending wrongful termination suit against Snopes\u8212 joined Binkowski to work at the rival site TruthOrFiction.org.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 In addition to legal woes and attribution issues, another, more troublesome albatross was hiding in plain sight at Snopes: Mikkelson couldn\u8217 t seem to bring himself to renounce his AFU-like games of cleverer-than-thou.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 This impulse to outwit and rile up folks felt weirdly at odds with the good faith and empathy you\u8217 d expect from someone in his business. In 2016, for example, Mikkelson kidded with Green on Slack that a man named Jeff Zarronandia was his best hire. \u8220 Model employee,\u8221  Green replied, according to screenshots. Mikkelson had made up Zarronandia a year before to troll the conservatives who insisted that Snopes was biased toward liberals. But as Snopes sought to level up, Green, then the director of business development, told Mikkelson that he thought they needed to \u8220 clean up our loose ends.\u8221  That didn\u8217 t happen, and Zarronandia was outed as an alt in a BuzzFeed expos\'e9 by the reporter Dean Sterling Jones.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Mikkelson didn\u8217 t exactly offer a mea culpa: \u8220 I mean, certainly, anyone who\u8217 s paying attention knows there\u8217 s no such thing as a Pulitzer Prize in numismatics,\u8221  he told Jones, referencing the made-up staffer\u8217 s made-up bio.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Trump advisor Roger Stone, who had referenced some of Zarronandia\u8217 s articles in his books, was livid when he found out. But he loved that Snopes had been discredited, and so did Fox News and Steve Bannon\u8217 s podcast War Room. Mikkelson had failed to see that the right wing would weaponize his behavior against not just Snopes, but all fact-checking orgs.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Another example involves a claim that humans swallow eight spiders per year in their sleep. Mikkelson had debunked it in a 2001 Snopes post, tracing it to a column in PC Professional by Lisa Birgit Holst.}{\rtlch\afs24
\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2
\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 But in time, people realized neither the magazine nor the columnist ever existed; and in 2015, a Reddit user figured out that the author\u8217 s name was anagrammatic. (\u8220 This is a big troll.\u8221 ) Mikkelson initially copped to nothing, but has since described the fictitious source as a \u8220 wink.\u8221  His explanation to alarmed staffers? He wanted to see if anyone was checking primary sources. \u8220 We\u8217 ve seen many instances where people [in a position like Mikkelson\u8217 s] say they\u8217 re \u8216 just checking to see if you\u8217 re paying attention,\u8217 \u8221  says the Shorenstein Center\u8217 s Dreyfuss. \u8220 It\u8217 s an old troll. And it\u8217 s completely unethical.\u8221 }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 I\u8217 ve heard from AFUers, Snopes fact-checkers, and other journalists that Mikkelson had to be the smartest guy in the room\u8212 that he came off as the guy who was way too interested in proving someone wrong. Staffers have colored him as a mudslinger and a gaslighter. They have said he was a black box who became a roi absent. Once an employee complained to their superior that talking to Mikkelson was \u8220 like going to see the wizard of Oz.\u8221  And a reputable business reporter, after spending an afternoon with Mikkelson, was struck, they told me, by how little Snopes\u8217  head seemed like management material.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 It\u8217 s a curious disconnect, given Mikkelson\u8217 s devotion to board games. In a rare Zoom meeting with a couple staffers in the summer of 2021, for example, he perked up excitedly when the conversation strayed to the subject of turning Snopes into a deduction board game \'e0 la Secret Hitler. \u8220 I have definite ideas about what I\u8217 d like a Snopes game to be and not be,\u8221  he said in the recording, obtained by Fast Company. He\u8217 d been playing Battlestar Galactica, based on the TV series, for seven years, multiple times a week. \u8220 It\u8217 s another hidden traitor mechanic,\u8221  he explained, beaming. \u8220 I kind of like that mechanic, again where there\u8217 s two teams, and you don\u8217 t know who\u8217 s on which team . . . \u8221 }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Mikkelson could often be found at board game conventions, in which he sometimes placed first or second, though Young had encouraged her husband to work instead on his leadership skills. \u8220 I even suggested puppy training and karate,\u8221  she says. (They divorced in 2022.)}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 In the end, Mikkelson was only half the equation: the other half, Vinny Green, was an extension of Mikkelson\u8217 s poor leadership, who came to hold day-to-day sway over Snopes\u8217  operations.}{\rtlch\afs24
\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2
\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Green had enlisted in the Marines at 17\u8212 an experience that he\u8217 s said exposed him to \u8220 a lot of leadership styles, good and bad.\u8221  He was finishing his associate degree in sociology at MiraCosta College when he turned up as a chatty friend-of-a-friend at the condo that Richmond and Schoentrup were renting in San Diego\u8217 s Ocean Beach neighborhood. \u8220 He seemed ambitious, which was cool,\u8221  said Schoentrup.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 In less than three years, Green shot from an internship with another of their companies, TV Tropes, to become Snopes\u8217  VP of operations. \u8220 I was 100% integral in getting Snopes as a client,\u8221  Green told me when we spoke in 2019. \u8220 David delegates all of operations to me.\u8221  (Though we spoke on the record all those years ago, Green declined a more recent request for an interview.) Mikkelson had agreed, too: \u8220 He was the guy coming up with all the ideas. He was the guy who was the most enthusiastic.\u8221 }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 \u8220 Most of what he did was tasks that weren\u8217 t specialized,\u8221  says Richmond in a less generous assessment. Richmond had never known anyone to form alliances as Green did. Like in one of Mikkelson\u8217 s board games, he and Schoentrup claim not to have realized the extent of the double-dealing until it was too late. They, and others, say that Green was in Mikkelson\u8217 s ear and blew up his relationship with Richmond and Schoentrup. Green told me they did that all by themselves.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Green seems to have cared a lot about rank. He pushed to be nominated for (and made) the Forbes 30 Under 30 List in 2017. \u8220 He thought he was just naturally good at this, that he picked up everything like a child genius,\u8221  LaCapria says.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 I\u8217 d first spoken to him in 2019, after Richmond and Schoentrup purchased Salon, and the prospect of VCs like them in journalism concerned the then-COO. \u8220 For the first time, they\u8217 ve got a newsroom under their purview,\u8221  Green said at the time.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Snopes was on a \u8220 death march . . . we\u8217 ve got a boot on our throat,\u8221  Green would go on, referring to the financial drain of the lawsuit with Proper Media. But big things like a membership account were coming down the pike: \u8220 We took Patreon and shoved it inside Snopes, took a subscription model and shoved it in, added a scrollable newsfeed and got to [Snopes\u8217 ] own platform.\u8221 }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Green has been described by colleagues as a temperamental mansplainer, \u8220 poser coder,\u8221  and \u8220 snake oil salesman\u8221  who talked a good game and had a desk stacked with books on leadership (including Radical Candor and Delivering Happiness: A Path to Profits, Passion, and Purpose). Ex-colleagues say he intercepted Binkowski\u8217 s invites to conferences and went in her stead. They also say he had \u8220 ideas for days\u8221  but was unable to follow through or evaluate what was working and what wasn\u8217 t.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Snopes teased the membership account in April 2019, for example. But it didn\u8217 t ship until November 2020\u8212 much too late\u8212 and was, according to Snopes\u8217  lead developer Chad Ort, both uninspired and over budget (he estimates they burned through $500,000 with outside developers). \u8220 I\u8217 ve heard him use the phrase \u8216 my gut\u8217  so many times and that just stops all conversations,\u8221  Ort complained to HR in one of a number of reports filed about Green, later obtained by Fast Company. \u8220 I keep asking for business requirements, and I never get them.\u8221 }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Employees say Green would lose his cool and bark orders, and would accuse staffers of subterfuge. \u8220 You need to stand down,\u8221  he once told a staffer that had been at Snopes since its dawn.}{\rtlch\afs24
\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2
\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 In April 2020, Carly Gillis started as director of operations and communications. She\u8217 d been raised as a Jehovah\u8217 s Witness, loved Snopes as a kid, and had worked in media for a decade. Given millennial nostalgia, she was surprised that Snopes had not pivoted into something bigger. Why, she wondered, weren\u8217 t they doing media literacy outreach? Why weren\u8217 t they on TikTok? \u8220 When I started to see the cracks was pretty quick,\u8221  she said. \u8220 David never initiated any business plans. It left Vinny scrambling.\u8221 }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 \u8220 What is so broken about this thing?\u8221  Lisa Wang, hired not long after Gillis as an operations manager, says she asked herself. She and Gillis saw that the problem was not the newsroom, which was doing solid work despite everything.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 [Source photo:}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb240\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\field{\*\fldinst{\rtlch\af0\alang1025\afs24
\ltrch\fs24\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0  HYPERLINK }{\rtlch\af0\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\fs24\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0  }{\rtlch\af0\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\fs24\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0 https://unsplash.com/@peppytoad}
