\ltrch\b0\i\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ul\cf1 Peppy Toad}}}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0
\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 /Unsplash]}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright
\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 One Friday, in April 2021, following a conversation that Wang and Ort had with Mikkelson by Zoom about Green, the company\u8217 s part-time HR consultant told Wang that an outside evaluator would be coming next week to audit Green\u8217 s performance, and that she\u8217 d be able to speak with them. That never happened. Instead, the following Thursday the entire operations team\u8212 Wang, Gillis, and their junior female colleague\u8212 were laid off. Financial strain was cited. (Finances were failing, but the decision also smacked of misogyny, which Wang and other women staffers say they experienced from both Mikkelson and Green.)}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 In August 2021, Buzzfeed contributor Dean Sterling Jones broke the story of Mikkelson having fabricated Zarronandia and using plagiarized material in at least 54 stories between 2015 and 2019. Mikkelson, who said he was trying to get copy out fast and \u8220 scoop up traffic,\u8221  was suspended from editorial, and an internal review counted a total of 194 articles that were plagiarized or poorly attributed.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Soon after Mikkelson\u8217 s black eye, Snopes\u8217  VP of advertising left for Fox News. And instead of reporting to Green, Ort began reporting to Doreen Marchionni, Snopes\u8217  managing editor since 2018. Marchionni was, according to everyone I spoke with, universally adored by the newsroom, but editorial could not check management.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Snopes\u8217  lead assignment editor left for CBS in May 2022; and by mid-June, a staff reporter emailed an ex-colleague to say that things at Snopes were \u8220 phenomenally bad.\u8221  Adding, \u8220 You were right about everything.\u8221 }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Senior employees were all working on reduced salaries. Reporters had been told that the company would go bust in a month. Reasons for that included OnTheIssues.org, a janky website that tracks the stances of politicians, which Snopes had acquired at Green\u8217 s suggestion back in 2019 and packaged as a bimonthly newsletter. \u8220 Where\u8217 s the business case? How will it make money?\u8221  Wang said she\u8217 d asked Green. \u8220 He came up with a lot of wild ideas that, in my opinion, were not grounded in reality.\u8221 }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Over the course of weeks and months, the reporters had helped Green work up various proposed fundraising solutions\u8212 a podcast, a logical fallacy flash-card game\u8212 only to have those projects shelved or binned without explanation. Their general manager\u8217 s latest strategy was a collectible coin drive. \u8220 Act now,\u8221  Green tweeted, \u8220 to get a . . . coin with a lifetime membership. We\u8217 re only making 7.5K. It\u8217 s like an NFT but real & you get ad-free browsing.\u8221  He\u8217 d told the newsroom that Snopes was going to make $750,000 from this, but the coins weren\u8217 t moving. One reporter vented in an email: \u8220 I can\u8217 t believe that we\u8217 re here and Vinny\u8217 s only idea is to sell collectible coins as though we\u8217 re daytime television advertising in the 1980s!!\u8221 }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The newsroom turned on Green in their last staff meetings, in which Mikkelson is said to have lurked in the background while his lieutenant took the heat. July neared: A different reporter composed a letter complaining about Green on behalf of the writers, and emailed it to Mikkelson with their blessings and the endorsement of editorial. It was a vote of no confidence. Finally, Green was fired, but by that point, three of the seven staff reporters had already jumped ship.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Then the pandemic hit. The reporters knew that every point of misinformation loomed like\u8212 or really was\u8212 a matter of life or death in that landscape. The tiny newsroom\u8217 s task was more Sisyphean and high stakes than ever, and traffic to the site regularly skyrocketed by well over 100%. Green had praised the staff for working \u8220 their asses off.\u8221  But meanwhile, thanks in part to his poor and unilateralist decisions,\~Snopes was on the ropes, even if the company\u8217 s mismanagement had been more easily obscured by the nature of an all-remote outfit and a managing editor in Marchionni who had done her best to shelter her team from tensions with the C-suite.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 But reporters were now seeing Snopes\u8217  situation as Wang had. \u8220 It\u8217 s being held hostage by these two men,\u8221  she\u8217 d said, \u8220 who are wildly incompetent at\u8212 wildly inappropriate for\u8212 their jobs.\u8221 }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Since 2017, the site\u8217 s part-owners and several of its past staffers have claimed that Mikkelson and Green were bad actors, hiding under the halo of fact-checking. Those sources were widely brushed aside as ax-grinders, squeaky wheels, competitors, and hysterical women\u8212 but they were right. That this did not come out sooner is an \u8220 indictment\u8221  of the media industry, Binkowski has said over and over.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Traffic to the site has continued to drop. To be fair, websites across the board have seen readership declines post-election and post-COVID, but even with that caveat, the numbers are jarring: Per Comscore, Snopes\u8217  traffic has declined from a monthly average of 32 million page views per month in 2020 to 9.6 million in 2021, and then 6.4 million last year.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 In\~early\~2022, Richmond and Schoentrup almost worked it out with Mikkelson. Reportedly, the snag was Green, who wished to find funding to buy and run Snopes himself.\~(Instead, he wound up founding a digital platform agency, called\~Web Multipliers.) Finally, in September 2022, Mikkelson sold his stake to Richmond and Schoentrup (who themselves had offloaded Proper Media in 2021), cutting all ties to Snopes. Three days later, Mikkelson married for a fourth time. Barbara settled Mikkelson\u8217 s related lawsuit against her as well, thus ending a hundred months of litigation between mom and pop.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Schoentrup told me that he and Richmond will \u8220 keep injecting money\u8221  into Snopes \u8220 until we save it.\u8221  So far, they have moved the site to a custom (read quick) CMS, with a redesign to follow. Snopes has also migrated off of unnecessary third-party tech vendors, which were costing it about $50k a month. (Salon, which has more traffic and employees, spends around $13k, Richmond said.) This January, Richmond coded a script that looked for Barbara\u8217 s internym in a 2015 backup and compared older articles to their versions on-site; if more than 50% of the text was the same, Barbara\u8217 s byline was restored\u8212 amounting to 1,427 articles. As Snopes CEO and president, the two are taking the same hands-off posture toward editorial that they have at Salon, which was profitable in 2020, 2021, and 2022.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 As the 2024 election nears, and the U.S. finds itself gripped by an unremitting informational crisis, the question is whether Snopes can still be the internet\u8217 s ombudsman. \u8220 I think, incredibly, [that this election] will be worse than the previous two for misinformation/disinformation,\u8221  says Marchionni, who has stayed on as managing and executive editor. But she believes that Snopes is ready: \u8220 We\u8217 re part of an NSF grant that is developing a tool to help newsrooms spot misinformation and stomp it out. And that\u8217 s been invigorating and fun. I think financially and morale-wise, we\u8217 re in the best shape we\u8217 ve been in in years, thank god. The newsroom earned it.\u8221 }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Schoentrup is the worrywart of the new leadership. As mediation dragged with Mikkelson and Green and the involvement of eight legal firms, he\u8217 d brooded over the damage done to America\u8217 s original fact-checking site. Then, one night, he rented Vengeance, the recent black comedy by B.J. Novak. Midway into the movie, he says he heard Novak\u8217 s character, a New Yorker journalist, flatly disagree with a cartel member, saying, \u8220 Go on Snopes. It\u8217 s not a real thing.\u8221 }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Dean Sterling Jones contributed reporting to this story.}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb240\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24
